web-preview/bundle.js

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
# The root tsconfig.json USED to be excluded here, on the grounds that the RN app
# build (Metro/Babel) does not read it. It has since become load-bearing: the
# typecheck gate reads it, and src/tsconfig.test.mjs runs the compiler against it.
# Cloning the repository proved the cost — a complete checkout with no root config
# and two failing gates. It is hand-written, not generated, so it belongs in here.
# The rule stays for tsconfigs anywhere else, which are generated.
tsconfig.json
!/tsconfig.json

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# What ./start and ./check write down. Useful on this machine, meaningless in the
# project, and they can contain a staff email address.
.local-logs/

# ── AND ANY LOG, ANYWHERE — 21 SEPTEMBER 2026 ──────────────────────────────
#
# The rule above named one directory, and the note on it already said logs "can
# contain a staff email address". A security sweep before this repository was
# first pushed found two that had walked straight past it:
# docs/measured/2026-09-18/{metro-run,backend}.log — 909 lines of a live
# shopping session on a real Zepto account, carrying the order handle, the order
# code, the product bought, the price paid and the machine's LAN address, all in
# one machine-readable file. They were removed; this is what stops the next one.
#
# A LOG IS A MEASUREMENT AND A MEASUREMENT BELONGS IN A COMMENT. This project
# already quotes the ONE line that mattered, redacted, beside the code it
# explains — that is the form a measurement takes here. A whole log file pasted
# into the repository is a record of what one identifiable person bought.
*.log

# ── THE APP'S OWN .env, WHICH WAS TRACKED ─────────────────────────────────
#
# Found by the same sweep. The rule below was `.env*.local` only, so plain
# `.env` was not ignored and WAS committed. It held one harmless line — a LAN
# address — but the rule everybody assumes exists did not exist, so the next
# person to put a key in it would have published it without being warned.
#
# backend/.env was always covered, by backend/.gitignore, and that is where the
# real secrets live. This closes the same door on this side.
#
# NOTHING BREAKS BY UNTRACKING IT: src/backend/apiBase.js works the address out
# from Metro at runtime and this file is only ever an override.
.env
